+	"repository": "pi",
+	"mode": "contract",
+	"evidence": [
+		{
+			"path": "packages/agent/test/harness/execution-tools.test.ts",
+			"symbol": "executeToolCall",
+			"start_line": 151,
+			"end_line": 171,
+			"observation": "The it.each case 'converts %s tool throws to error output' drives both a synchronous throw and an asynchronous throw through executeToolCall(cleared, effectGate(), ...) and asserts result.isError === true plus the failure text 'tool failed'. This is the public acceptance contract for the failed-effect path: a tool effect that throws is normalized to a durable-error result, i.e. it can never fall through as an unflagged success."
+		},
+		{
